My current Samuri is doing very, very well: 366 hit points, AC
-26 and more possible, GDSM, helm of brillance and robe, etc.
for spellcasting, two weaponing a +6 Excalibur and a +4 katana,
with Grayswandir waiting to be charged up (and already used
against silver haters), already found the vibrating square and
marked it, etc.  In sum, my first ascention is looking possible,
except for one minor detail.  I had a slight accident with a bag
of holding and a wand of cancelation in mid-game: I'd already
seen the castle and about half Gehennom, when I needed to renew
my spells.  My spellbooks were all in my original cache, at
level 2, so while I was up there, I thought I'd take advantage
of the fact, and move anything that I would be needing in
Gehennom down to a lower stash.  So shovelling all sorts of odds
and ends into my bag of holding, I stumbled accross a wand of
cancelation that I was sure I didn't have.

Amongst the other things I'd already put into the sack was the
wand of wishing from the castle (unused!, and the only one seen
in this game), and my candles.  And a lot of other stuff, of
course.  I've managed to get back most of what I need, but when
it comes to candles, Izchak only had four more, and I've
stumbled accross two others in the depths, but that leaves me
one short.

I've since cleared out everything in the dungeon except the
Wizard himself (and of course, Moloch's sanctum).  I could just
wander around, hoping to get another candle, but I've already
read most of my spellbooks twice, and since I'm using them as my
main ranged weapon...  So just what are the ways of getting a
candle:
 -- just getting lucky and finding one (hasn't worked so far),
 -- a wand of wishing (a waste, but since I haven't found any
    wands of wishing other than the one in the castle, academic
    anyway),
 -- a wand of polymorph on a pile of tools (but I've only seen
    one wand of polymorph so far, and I used that up trying to
    get some decent armor, before realizing that an ordinary
    helmet or an old pot will never turn into a helm of
    brilliance),
 -- ???
Is there anything else I should be looking for, or trying to do?
(I do have a magic marker, and lot's of blanked scrolls.  But I
don't see off hand how that helps.)

FWIW: the RGN seems to have been acting very strange in this
game.  The last time I got anywhere near this far, I had scrolls
of enchant armor/weapon to spare -- this time, they've been
exceedingly rare, to the point that I still have Grayswandir at
only +1, the same as my T-shirt, and my levitation boots haven't
even been foo-proofed.  (The speed boots that I normally wear
have been, of course.)  I've also seen 0 scrolls of gold
detection, at least since the accident with the BoH.  At least
it's been generous with the wands of death -- I lost three in
the accident, but have found three others since then.  Which
will be, I hope, enough for Rodney, if I ever find another
candle.

